  "summary": "Web rendering is detached from database, native-auth, provider and job authority through fixed Core HTTP reads, an explicit command registry and preserved native protocol routes. A credential-free conventional Next production build and source/output graphs verify frontend import separation. An isolated production Next/Core/native PostgreSQL proof exercised authenticated SSR, a real thin Server Action cookie roundtrip, native auth relay, persisted commands, CSRF and cross-owner denials, metadata refresh and clean producer shutdown. Independent exact-diff source review covered the extraction and all final follow-ons without actionable findings.",
  "limitations": "Source and isolated local runtime qualification only. Native behavior ran at 7f9b9a927c4385ee0812b83f5d8a30ed2204ae45 with package 1.7.2; d1ecfa99e1dd93d35643fcffb312c9ce3e94590e adds version/release metadata, newsletter environment ownership, the restored Web deployment stamp and formatting-only handler/harness changes. The final 1.8.1 credential-free build used those same final source bytes, with APP_COMMIT still identifying the preceding checkout. The independent reviewer inspected source and retained evidence declarations; they did not rerun the application. An earlier bounded full-unit campaign did not finish. Full hosted application/PostgreSQL suites, Chromium qualification and all four CodeQL analyses remain separate required exact-main publication gates. No container/retained-installation, production deployment, Cloudflare adapter, provider delivery, tenancy, complete human journey or customer acceptance is claimed. Newsletter activation, subscriber intake and sending remain deferred.",
